From: =?UTF-8?q?Petr=20=C5=A0tetiar?= <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 06:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] nl80211: validate radio-local hostapd removal targets
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A reused MLD socket path can remain associated with an AP of another
radio. The 0004 preflight then correctly refuses its foreign owner:

  bss wlan1.2 (wlan1.2_link0) is held by iface of unknown bss wlan0.1_link0, abort radio removal

Build the removal set from loaded identity instead of saved client
paths. Exclude unresolved sockets individually. Preserve the
conservative guard when partial radio/BSSID evidence or a saved local
association makes an unresolved socket a candidate for this radio.
Unrelated transients do not prevent removing known local interfaces or
accepting an empty local set.

Retain 0004's local first-BSS owner and self-membership checks. Validate
all local candidates before issuing commands, then re-resolve each owner
before SET and recheck its BSSID and inode before REMOVE. Use temporary
clients for those verified targets; removal does not close or rebind any
manager's live connections.

Signed-off-by: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
---
